      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for those. honestly some of them feel a bit heavy/formal for a mobile app (like \"unveil your ledger\" is a bit much lol), but i get what you're doing with the verb stacking to hit the metric. \n\ncan we try to push the score even higher though? i want to see what happens if we really crank up the energy. instead of just two verbs, try to pack as many high-action, high-energy verbs into each label as possible. let's see how high we can actually get that score for these same 5 actions. \n\n1. checking your account balance\n2. sending money to a friend\n3. paying a monthly bill\n4. looking at transaction history\n5. setting up a savings goal",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
